{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 c6 6. Bc4 Bf5 7. Bd2 e6 8. O-O Nbd7 9. Qe2 Bb4 10. a3 Bxc3 11. Bxc3 { Laboratory starts here. Black develops the light-squared bishop before closing the diagonal with ...e6. ...c6 gives the queen c7 as a possible retreat and restrains Nb5. Develop the f8 bishop, choose a safe king destination and connect the rooks. Watch for a useful ...c5 or ...e5 break after development. } 11... Qd8 { Candidate comparison. Places the queen on d8. Compare its activity and safety with its previous square, then use the branch explanation to connect the move to a plan. } 12. a4 O-O 13. a5 Qc7 14. h3 h6 15. Bd2 Rfd8 { Candidate comparison. Places the rook on d8. Compare its activity and safety with its previous square, then use the branch explanation to connect the move to a plan. } 16. Rfc1 Be4 17. b4 e5 18. Nxe5 Nxe5 19. dxe5 Qxe5 { Candidate comparison. The queen captures a pawn on e5. Calculate the best reply before assuming a recapture, then recount material and opened lines. } 20. Bb3 Qb5 21. Re1 *

