{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Bf5 6. Ne5 c6 7. g4 Be6 8. Bc4 Nbd7 9. Bxe6 Nxe5 10. Qe2 Ng6 11. Bb3 { Laboratory starts here. Be6 saves the bishop and avoids the immediate h4 chase that can follow a retreat to g6. The engine comparison favors this retreat in the exact position shown. Complete development and inspect the center before counterattacking the advanced pawns. Keep the queen safe from discovered attacks as White's knight moves. } 11... h5 { Candidate comparison. Creates a wing or central pawn contact and changes king shelter. Calculate captures and the opponent's central counterplay before extending the advance. } 12. g5 Nd5 13. Bd2 Nxc3 14. Qd3 Nh4 15. g6 Nxg6 { Candidate comparison. The knight captures a pawn on g6. Calculate the best reply before assuming a recapture, then recount material and opened lines. } 16. bxc3 Rd8 17. Rg1 Ne5 18. Qe2 Ng4 19. O-O-O g6 { Candidate comparison. Prepares a fianchetto and changes the long diagonal. Check the bishop and corner rook before assuming the next developing move is safe. } 20. Rde1 Rh7 21. Kb2 *

